findings.claim:
doc87ContextFrames accepts only the 'SQL statement "' and 'SQL expression "' wrappers. It rejects these PG 14+ renderings:
- 'PL/pgSQL assignment "..."', used for any non-simple assignment;
- the bare 'SQL function "x"' form;
- lineless PL/pgSQL frames ('PL/pgSQL function f(...) while casting return value...').

A wrapper also ends early at any SQL-text line that ends with a double quote.

None of these occurs on the reasoned admin, replay or readiness marker stacks:
- admin_detail:178 and readiness assignments are simple expressions;
- replay:296 uses PERFORM, rendered as SQL statement;
- readiness uses a SELECT INTO wrapper.

A canonical or currentness change could make a control unpassable, and the 'SQL and PL/pgSQL renderings' wording in authoredDiagnosticControls overstates what the fixtures cover. Fail-closed, not a false pass.

